intonation: period phrase matches final bang (drop IBM's)

period_phrase matches a final mark of kind 13 and gives it no special
assignment of its own; exclamation carries kind 4. Matching kind 4
here as well sends `!' down the period path from the start: no
question probe, no exclamation probe and their backtracks, and the
generic sentence-final path then processes the utterance exactly as
it processes `.'. Together with no-exclam (0017) nothing IBM did for
`!' remains in force. The mark itself is untouched.

diff --git a/lang/enus/rules/ut_inton.dr b/lang/enus/rules/ut_inton.dr
--- a/lang/enus/rules/ut_inton.dr
+++ b/lang/enus/rules/ut_inton.dr
@@ -1000,5 +1000,7 @@
   load movw statefld 1546 into r0w
   popn 7
   cmp cmpw statefld 1514 reg r0w
   branch je to L2
+  cmp cmpw imm 4 statefld 1514
+  branch je to L2
 label L1 was at_0x79
   push imm 94
